@page "/"

<PageTitle>Backlog UI Storybook</PageTitle>

<StoryPage Title="Backlog UI Storybook"
           Summary="Every component in Backlog.UI.Components, rendered on its own.">

    <Story Name="What this is"
           Description="Why the library exists and what this host is for.">
        <div class="sb-stack">
            <p>
                <code>Backlog.UI.Components</code> is a Razor Class Library with no domain in it.
                It knows about buttons, inputs, markdown blocks and tree rows — it does not know
                about entries, backlogs or repositories. Anything that would need that vocabulary
                stays in the app.
            </p>
            <p>
                This storybook references the library and <code>Backlog.Aspire.ServiceDefaults</code>
                and nothing else. If a component ever grew a dependency on a module, this project
                would stop compiling — which is the cheapest possible test of that boundary.
            </p>
            <p>
                It is also the surface to review the components on: they render here exactly as
                they render in the app, because the storybook links the library stylesheet and
                adds only page chrome of its own.
            </p>
        </div>
    </Story>

    <Story Name="How to run it"
           Description="Standalone, or as an Aspire resource next to the other harnesses."
           Code="@RunCode">
        <div class="sb-stack">
            <p>
                Under the AppHost it is the <code>ui-storybook</code> resource. It starts
                automatically and waits for nothing, because it depends on nothing.
            </p>
            <p>
                Standalone, Kestrel picks the port and prints it. Diagrams fetch mermaid and
                G6 from a CDN on first use, so on a machine with no egress the
                <a href="diagrams">Diagrams</a> and <a href="graph-explorer">Graph explorer</a>
                pages fall back to showing their source instead of a picture. Everything else
                renders offline.
            </p>
        </div>
    </Story>

    <Story Name="Component groups"
           Description="Grouped by what the components do. Foundations comes first: everything below is built from those tokens.">
        @* The loop variable is not called "page": Razor reads @page.Href as the
           @page directive and the file stops compiling. *@
        <div class="sb-grid">
            @foreach (var link in StorybookIndex.ComponentPages)
            {
                <a class="sb-card-link" href="@link.Href">
                    <span class="sb-card-link__title">@link.Title</span>
                    <span class="sb-card-link__text">@link.Summary</span>
                </a>
            }
        </div>
    </Story>

</StoryPage>

@code {
    private const string RunCode = """
        # standalone
        dotnet run --project src/harness/Backlog.UI.Storybook

        # with everything else
        aspire run
        """;
}
